{
  "slug": "epic-harness",
  "name": "Epic Harness",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin that replaces 30+ commands with 6, auto-triggers skills based on what you're doing, and evolves new skills from your own failure patterns. Less surface area to memorize. More intelligence per keystroke.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **27 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (27): `_critic` (HarnessX Critic (Tier 2.1) — adversarial review of evolved-skill proposals against trace evidence), `_dispatch` (Core router), `agent-introspection` (Loop-breaking self-diagnosis), `audit` (Audit phase), `commit` (Conventional Commits 1.0 generator), `context` (Context window manager), `council` (4-voice parallel deliberation (Architect · Skeptic · Pragmatist · Critic) for architecture, tech selection, or design decisions with…), `debug` (Systematic root-cause isolation for test failures, runtime errors, or unexpected behavior), and 19 more\n- **MCP servers** (1): `harness-mem`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install epic-harness@claude-community` from `epicsagas/epic-harness`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 27,
    "mcp": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
